Faxbot: the built-in engine sends the subaddress (SUB) a fax asks for (spandsp 0.0.6).

T.33 routing names a department or mailbox behind one fax number by the
subaddress the sender states, and a notice fax to an enrolled partner carries
its 20-digit notice ID the same way (direct/notice.py). The SSL Fax engine
already sends one (hfaxd's JPARM SUBADDR); the built-in engine could not.

With FAXBOT_TX_SUB on the channel (ami.py sets it on the Originate), SendFAX
hands it to spandsp (t30_set_tx_sub_address), on audio and T.38 calls alike,
after faxbot_sub_clean in faxbot_t38_gateway.h keeps only what a subaddress
may hold: digits and +, # and *, at most 20. Anything else sends nothing and
logs one WARNING. spandsp sends SUB with its DCS only when the far end's DIS
says it takes subaddresses (DIS bit 49), so Faxbot records the subaddress as
requested, and as carried only when that bit was set (engine_frames.py). One
NOTICE line per session names the subaddress. A sent fax without FAXBOT_TX_SUB
is unchanged.

Receiving: spandsp 0.0.6's own DIS leaves bit 49 clear (its default T.30
features have no subaddressing), so a sending machine that honours the DIS
never sent the built-in engine a SUB, and receiving rules by subaddress and
notice pairing by SUB could not work there. A fax this engine receives now
says it takes one (faxbot_receive_subaddress). The replay proof in
asterisk/tests shows SUB carried with the bit and withheld without it.

--- a/res/res_fax_spandsp.c
+++ b/res/res_fax_spandsp.c
@@ -1203,6 +1203,31 @@
 	t30_set_phase_e_handler(p->t30_state, t30_phase_e_handler, s);
 	/* Faxbot (0004): keep the frames both sides send, for the channel variables at the end of the session. */
 	t30_set_real_time_frame_handler(p->t30_state, faxbot_frame_handler, p);
+	/* Faxbot (0005): the T.33 subaddress (SUB) this fax asks for (FAXBOT_TX_SUB), on audio and T.38 alike. spandsp
+	 * sends it only when the far end's DIS says it takes one, so Faxbot records it as requested, not as carried. */
+	if (s->chan && (s->details->caps & AST_FAX_TECH_SEND)) {
+		const char *asked;
+		char sub[FAXBOT_SUB_MAX + 1];
+		int given;
+
+		ast_channel_lock(s->chan);
+		asked = pbx_builtin_getvar_helper(s->chan, "FAXBOT_TX_SUB");
+		given = asked && *asked;
+		faxbot_sub_clean(asked, sub, sizeof(sub));
+		ast_channel_unlock(s->chan);
+		if (sub[0]) {
+			t30_set_tx_sub_address(p->t30_state, sub);
+			ast_log(LOG_NOTICE, "Faxbot: subaddress %s requested on %s\n", sub, ast_channel_name(s->chan));
+		} else if (given) {
+			ast_log(LOG_WARNING, "Faxbot: the subaddress for %s is not one a fax can carry; none is sent\n",
+				ast_channel_name(s->chan));
+		}
+	}
+	/* Faxbot (0005): a fax this engine receives says it takes a subaddress (DIS bit 49), which spandsp leaves out by
+	 * default, so a sending machine that honours the DIS sends its SUB (receiving rules by subaddress). */
+	if (s->details->caps & AST_FAX_TECH_RECEIVE) {
+		faxbot_receive_subaddress(p->t30_state);
+	}
 
 	/* set T.38 parameters */
 	if (p->ist38) {
